 "mode": "L1X_ACT_SERVE (development; descriptive; nothing chosen)",
 "definitions": "L1X -- SELECT lane, step 12: the WebQSP twin of _l1x_actserve.py (generated by _mk_actserve_wq.py): how far does ONE static A^T x reach on WebQSP when it is fed more FLAT hits (ACT) and ranks a larger pool?  (development only; nothing is chosen here)\n(User ruling 2026-10-01: L1 = parameter-free routing and SELECTION only -- no traversal, no fitted or learned rule.   User 2026-10-02: \"try expanding metaqa oracle and improving the all coverage\"; 2026-10-03 \"yeah do those things ... also l1 improvements\".)\n\nThe shipped IR_L1 feeds the one-hop localisation with the top ACT = 200 FLAT hits and ranks the pool O[:5000].  The reach study (probe_reach) showed the one-hop support of the top-ACT hits covers\nALL golds on 54% (ACT 200), 64% (500), 70% (1000) and 77% (3000) of the MetaQA rows, so the single-product oracle can be expanded.  Here the WHOLE routed pipeline is re-run with (ACT, POOL):\n  hits         top-ACT of FLAT, weight 1/(rank+1) * g        (as shipped)\n  O            RRF(FLAT, LOC), K0 = 60;  pool = O[:POOL]\n  router       ES (shipped) or ES_c (typed order, the L1_TYPED_SELECT_CANDIDATE order) over V_q = hits U LOC;  count B_P(q,K): the shipped knee/alpha rule applied to the SAME hit set ('own'), or the count of the\n               ACT = 200 run ('ref', i.e. the shipped count with only the order/ranking fed by more hits)\n  served       SHIPPED (O) or TYP = RRF(Sro, Sri, Tin) over the pool (equal weight, K0 = 60);  a gold outside the pool is placed at its exact O position (as in _l1x_rrt_route.py)\nIdentities for ACT = 200, POOL = 5000: (ES, SHIPPED, own) == the stored kscale verdict on every (row, B_N) and B_P == the stored count.  Half A = even rows, half B = odd rows; everything is also split by hop.\n\n  python -u scratchpad/_l1x_actserve_wq.py RUN webqsp <tag> [--rows=K]   -> results/L1_X/actserve_webqsp__<tag>.{json,npz}  (write-once)\n  python -u scratchpad/_l1x_actserve_wq.py SHOW <tag> [K]                (prints half B, per configuration)\nIdentities for ACT = 200, POOL = 5000 on WebQSP: (ES, SHIPPED, own) == the stored CALIB_EVAL_WEBQSP verdict (SV__PHG__k<K>__own == #gold) and B_P == BP__PHG__k<K>__own on every row.\n",
